## 2. MLOps Platforms & Infrastructure

### 2.1 Atlassian's ML Platform Architecture (Standard Path FY25-26)

The end-to-end ML framework at Atlassian follows a left-to-right pipeline:

1. **Data Lake & Feature Stores** — Socrates tables, Tecton feature views, MLFS
2. **Training & Experimentation** — Databricks notebooks, MLflow experiments and runs
3. **Workflow Orchestration (ML Studio)** — Workflows as DAGs of modules (data prep, training, evaluation, packaging, registration)
4. **Model Registry & Serving Control Plane** — MSP / Tarot v3 model registry; ML Registry for lineage; Deployment Store for artifact replication
5. **Serving Backends** — SageMaker endpoints and TEAMServe Triton instances
6. **Product Services (Micros)** — Service descriptors referencing MSP model groups/versions
7. **Observability** — ML Lens, SignalFx, Splunk

[End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202046686c7c93274f379403a2283d58293f/pages/6708596091/End-to-End+ML+Framework+Atlassian)

### 2.2 Praxis ML — Unified Training Framework

**Praxis ML** is Atlassian's emerging unified training framework providing:

- **Trainer**: Abstracts training logic; extensible for different ML/LLM tasks
- **Evaluator**: Standardizes evaluation and batch inference workflows
- **Deployer**: Handles deployment logic for model serving
- **Recipes**: Preconfigured Python scripts for common training/evaluation tasks
- **CLI Tool**: Unified interface for launching, monitoring, and managing jobs
- **Job Scheduler**: Integrates with Kubernetes (via Kueue) for remote/distributed execution
- **Integrations**: Hooks for Ray, Weights & Biases, and other third-party tools

Key value proposition: The interactive and production paths share the same recipes, configs, and submission model — minimizing duplication, drift, and handoffs between experimentation and production.

[Praxis ML: Atlassian Unified Training Surface](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/es33tss22axj/pages/6956392087/Praxis+ML+Atlassian+Unified+Training+Surface)
[Praxis-ML One-Pager](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/es33tss22axj/pages/7003858857/Praxis-ML+One-Pager)

### 2.3 ML Studio — Workflow Orchestration

ML Studio is Atlassian's dedicated platform for ML model development:

**Key Capabilities:**
- YAML-based workflow definitions (DAGs of modules)
- Three execution modes: **adhoc**, **experimental**, **released**
- Integration with MLflow for experiment tracking
- Continuous training and automated deployment
- Data governance and privacy controls
- ~2,400 workflow files, ~1,300 library files

**Key Technologies:**
- Python3.12, Databricks (Spark-based), Bitbucket Pipelines CI/CD
- ML Frameworks: HuggingFace, PyTorch, custom implementations
- Data: Delta tables, Socrates (data lake)

**Workflow Descriptor Example:**
```yaml
name: srobilliard-test-modules-released
use_case: ml_studio_testing_ml_platform
team: ML Platform
module_tasks:
  - step_name: "module-1"
    module: "example_module"
    version: "2.3.5"
    parameters:
      - name: variable_1
        value: 1
platforms:
  - name: "default_cluster"
    type: databricks/spark
    runtime: 13.3.x-cpu-ml-scala2.12
    instance_type: m5.2xlarge
```

[ML Studio Introduction](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020e8e542e6fbb547dea43317e50413b60f/pages/4166496993/ML+Studio+Introduction)
[ML Studio: Workflow Orchestration Overview](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/3243638104/ML+Studio+Workflow+Orchestration+Overview)

### 2.4 Future Architecture: ML Fabric on Kubernetes

The ML Platform is evolving toward Kubernetes-based orchestration:

- **Argo Workflows** for DAG orchestration, conditional branching, loops
- **MLflow** for experiment memory, run comparison, model versioning
- **Karpenter** for GPU-on-demand provisioning (A10G/H100)
- **RayJob, PyTorchJob, SparkApplication** as execution backends
- **CronWorkflows** for scheduled retraining
- **Argo Events** for drift-detection-triggered retraining

[ML Orchestration Roadmap: From Databricks to ML Fabric on Kubernetes](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202091e93be306a64a9b8d5e1faf780e8820/pages/7013482971)

