## 7. Model Deployment & Lifecycle

### 7.1 Deployment Flow

1. **Training** → Databricks/ML Studio produces model artifact
2. **Registration** → Upload to ML Registry (Tarot v3) with compliance validation
3. **Packaging** → Model artifacts bundled (tar.gz for SageMaker, unzipped for Triton)
4. **Deployment Compliance** → DMP Gatekeeper validates artifact compliance
5. **Deployment** → Service descriptor (`.sd.yml`) declares model endpoint
6. **Serving** → SageMaker or TEAMServe instance serves traffic

### 7.2 Service Descriptor Pattern

Models are deployed via Micros service descriptors:
- SageMaker: Real-time inference endpoints
- TEAMServe: GPU-aware, multi-model Triton instances
- Referenced by MSP model groups and versionTags

### 7.3 Rollback Procedures

- Feature flags for gradual rollout (`platform_enable_teamserve_streaming`, etc.)
- Shadow testing before production cutover
- Champion/challenger model patterns
- Auto-scaling policies (SageMaker) with tunable parameters

[Model Serving Platform Integration - Project Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/VAPPDEV/pages/2617527080)

