## 3. Experiment Tracking & Model Registry

### 3.1 MLflow (Primary Experiment Tracker)

MLflow is integrated with Databricks for:

| Feature | Usage Pattern |
|---------|--------------|
| **Run Management** | Each workflow execution creates a run under an experiment |
| **Experiment Tracking** | `mlflow.log_param()`, `mlflow.log_metric()`, `mlflow.log_artifact()` |
| **Artifact Storage** | Files, datasets, configs associated with runs |
| **Model Registry** | Registers/versions/stages models: `mlflow.pytorch.log_model()` |
| **Auto-logging** | GPU utilization, memory, CPU via system metrics |
| **Parent/Child Runs** | Nested runs for hyperparameter sweeps |

**Tracking URI pattern:** `databricks://socrates-public:ml-databricks`
**Experiment paths:** `/Teams/{team-name}/{experiment_name}` or `/mlflow/released/{region}/{domain}/{experiment}`

[MLflow in Databricks](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PDS/pages/3010137469/MLflow+in+Databricks)
[Building ML Models in vNext with MLFlow: A Complete Template](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/VOLTRON/pages/5924157618)

### 3.2 Weights & Biases (W&B)

Used via Praxis ML integration for:
- Distributed training monitoring
- Experiment comparison and visualization
- Integration alongside MLflow in certain teams

[RFC: Praxis ML Components and Usage Patterns](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~701218ab3150018744a9bb1a7851d5c51d5b3/pages/6076184287)

### 3.3 Agentic ML Experiment Loop (mlexp)

A lightweight, developer-first system for experiment tracking:
- CLI tool (`mlexp`) for listing, showing, diffing, syncing experiments
- Local experiment log (`~/.mlexp/experiments.jsonl`)
- Streamlit query-level eval tool
- Rovo Dev AI agent skill integration

[Agentic ML Experiment Loop](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020d2e2445580da4d86b9e6a5e346190367/pages/6722400136)

### 3.4 ML Registry (Tarot v3)

Tarot is Atlassian's model registry service with:

**Data Model:**
- **Namespace** → **Component** (type + owner) → **Version** (group of artifacts) → **Artifacts** (files with metadata)
- Component types: `model`, `prompt`, `dataset`, `sagemaker-package`, `module`

**Compliance Features:**
- PRGB (Peer Review + Green Build) compliance enforcement
- Artifact compliance attestations via DMP (Deployment Metadata Platform)
- Data classification labels (RED/ORANGE/YELLOW/GREEN/WHITE enclaves)
- Non-compliant artifacts blocked from production deployment

**Sources of Compliant Artifacts:**
- Bitbucket pipeline on compliant branch
- ML Studio released workflow
- **Non-compliant:** Ad-hoc workflows, experimental workflows, local machine uploads

[ML Registry <-> DMP Documentation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5156816091)
[[Draft] ML Model Deployment Flow](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6023156525)

