## 5. Evaluation Frameworks

### 5.1 AIX-Eval (Internal Evaluation Framework)

`atlassian-ai-experience-evaluation` (aixeval) is the primary internal evaluation framework:

**Modes:**
- **Evaluate**: Run evaluation metrics against datasets with pre-existing LLM outputs
- **Generate**: Generate LLM responses based on custom model/config settings

**Key Features:**
- LLM-as-a-judge metrics alongside traditional NLP metrics
- Integration with AI Gateway for model access
- Results logging to MLflow
- **Evaluations as Code (EVaC)**: YAML-based configuration —2lines of Python + config file

**Supported environments:** Local, Databricks notebooks, ML Studio

[AIX-Eval](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120203bd0205883eb4c12af95fe0e997be99f/pages/6522081308/AIX-Eval)

### 5.2 Rovo-Eval

Internal evaluation framework for Rovo-specific AI features, preferred over external solutions for:
- Reduced implementation complexity
- Better integration with Atlassian infrastructure
- Lower vendor dependency risk

[SPIKE: ML Evaluation Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202036af61f960604897b3e8da6cda3794c0/pages/6098222361)

### 5.3 Evaluation Metrics Used

**Ranking Models:** MRR@K, NDCG@K (K=1,3,5,10,10000)
**Classification:** Precision, Recall, F1, AUC, Accuracy
**LLM Evaluation:** LLM-as-judge, faithfulness, relevance, coherence
**Recommender Systems:** CTR, diversity, coverage, IPS/DR estimators
**Feature Importance:** SHAP values, LIME explanations

[Default stack L2 March-Apr Offline Experiment Logs](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/rdm/pages/6486952033)
[FY26Q4 EWS Model Performance Evaluation](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020a2953c1f5bf3459f9bbaba57e976cd23/pages/6855099772)

### 5.4 MSR Evaluation SDK

Purpose-built for multi-stage recommender evaluation:
- User-centric ranking metrics (precision/recall at K, NDCG)
- Item-centric ranking metrics (for marketing/NBP use cases)
- Segment-aware analysis at different granularity
- PySpark MLlib integration for scalability

[MSR Evaluation SDK Design Proposal](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/5566528850)

