## 6. Model Monitoring & Observability

### 6.1 ML Lens (Platformized ML Observability)

ML Lens is the ML Platform's cross-cutting observability platform:

**Capabilities:**
- **Metric ingestion API** for pushing values
- **Time-series metric store** (backed by Observo)
- **Alerting engine** with Slack and OpsGenie integrations
- **Visualization UI** for charting, comparing runs, slicing by tags

**Observability Pillars:**
| Pillar | Coverage |
|--------|----------|
| Data Observability | Data shifts, profiling, UGC metadata analysis |
| Feature Observability | Feature distribution drifts vs training reference |
| Training Observability | Automated data profiling, metric comparison |
| Prediction Observability | Model input/feature drift in near real-time |
| Tracing | Lineage graph linking models → workflows → tables → modules |

**Alert Configuration Example:**
```json
{
  "metric_key": "row_count_for_confluence_page",
  "namespace": "abc",
  "expectations": [{"operator": ">=", "expected_value": 900}],
  "anomaly_detections": [{"algorithm": "confidence_band", "config": {"sensitivity": 2}}],
  "alerts": [{"type": "jsm_ops", "values": ["eng-ml-platform"]}, {"type": "slack", "values": ["#ml-platform"]}]
}
```

[Platformized ML Observability - ML Lens](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5750038712)
[ML Observability - High Level Architecture](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/4383629681)

### 6.2 Drift Detection

**Types monitored:**
- **Data Drift (Feature Drift)**: Statistical property changes in input data (PSI, KS tests)
- **Label Drift (Concept Drift)**: Target variable distribution changes
- **Model Drift**: Performance degradation over time

**Architecture decision:** Drift detection belongs in the **Features pillar** (ML Lens / MLFS) rather than the Training pillar (ML Studio), as it's fundamentally a feature observability concern.

**Key metrics:** Time to Detection, Time to Resolution

**Tools used:**EvidentlyAI (open-source), scipy, alibi-detect, custom implementations

[ML Observability for Growth Recommendations: Needs, Gaps, and Path Forward](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6650192184)

### 6.3 Retraining Triggers

- **Scheduled**: Databricks CRON,Argo CronWorkflows (weekly/nightly)
- **Event-driven**: Drift detection → automatic retraining via Argo Events
- **Manual**: MLEs trigger ad-hoc retraining when performance issues are identified
- **Threshold-based**: Metric drops below configured thresholds trigger alerts + automated mitigation

